architecture estate-edition
  canonical_name EstateEdition
  family surface
  domain Surface / What this estate has to show today
  layer presentation
  semantic_question If this estate has read sixty-nine thousand things, what does it have to show for it today -- as a publication, not as a feed?
  purpose One dated edition composed from material the estate already kept, dressed in a presentation template the estate actually published. A cover, a strip of photographs, something to watch, something to listen to, and a reading list, each piece carrying who published it and when it was read.
  maturity implemented
  node_types Edition
  node_types EditionPiece
  node_types PresentationTemplate
  edge_types composed_from
  edge_types dressed_by
  internal_calculus the design is not invented for the occasion: it is chosen from the presentation templates this estate has actually published, restricted to the magazine family that carries a full set of layout tokens, and rotated by the day so the edition changes its clothes without anyone dressing it. The page names the template it is wearing
  internal_calculus every selection is bounded to a sane window of the last forty-five days, because timestamps in the archive span 1970 to 2105 and an unbounded order by date hands the cover to whichever feed has the worst clock
  internal_calculus one headline appears once. A feed that republishes the same item hourly would otherwise take three slots in an edition, so the reading list groups by the title itself
  internal_calculus a title is printed as its publisher meant it rather than as its encoder left it: feeds arrive having escaped their own quotation marks, sometimes several times over, and the escaping is collapsed until it stops changing
  invariant every piece is material this estate already read and kept; the composer fetches nothing at compose time and generates no text of its own
  invariant a standing publish pass reads the retained archive and published design once, then emits the edition for each declared public territory and the live root route
  forbidden_inference a piece appearing in the edition -> this estate endorsing it, vouching for it, or judging it worth reading
  forbidden_inference a piece appearing in the edition -> its source still publishing it, or what it says being true
  forbidden_inference the template's name on the page -> the theme's authors knowing this estate exists or approving of this use
  forbidden_inference an edition existing -> an editor; nothing here was chosen by a person
  source_path scripts/publish-edition.mjs
  source_path scripts/edition-policy.cue
  source_path scripts/edition.css
  source_path scripts/publish_estate.sh
  source_path scripts/publish_edition.py.archive
  witness scripts/tests/publish_edition.test.mjs proves the native compiler selects retained material inside the declared time windows, wears a published magazine profile, preserves attribution and the cannot-infer boundary, refuses unsafe CSS tokens, stages independently of the repo, and matched the retired Python semantic receipt on a fixture before cutover
  witness scripts/tests/publish_estate_native_entrypoints_test.sh guards the standing publisher against a direct Python entrypoint and includes the native edition compiler; the edition fixture proves one read emits the root route and all four declared territory routes
  witness 2026-09-25 published to all four territories: template "fern magazine, loud dusk", a real photographic cover, a three-photograph strip, one video, four audio pieces and fourteen deduplicated headlines, over 69,132 things kept from 1,667 publishers, with 32 days of keeping charted
  witness 2026-09-25 verified in a browser on aurekai.live/edition: real photography at full bleed, mono bylines naming publisher and time under every piece, the chart drawn by the time organ, and no escaped quotation mark left anywhere in the rendered text
  known_gap the edition is the estate's own; no subject gets an edition of what was kept under their address yet
  known_gap the cover is the most recent thing with an image inside the sane window, which is recency rather than judgment, and the page does not claim otherwise
  known_gap the daily rotation of the template is arithmetic on the day number, so two consecutive days can land on templates that look alike
  known_gap the native edition has a fixture and staging witness, not a replay of all four live territories or a browser check after cutover
  interacts edition-wears-the-organs

interaction edition-wears-the-organs
  source estate-edition
  destination client-organs
  relation enhances_without_composing
  preserves the composer as the only thing that decides what the edition says; the organs animate, anchor and chart what is already in the page
  drops any path by which the browser could choose a piece, reorder the edition, or fetch material
  forbidden_inference a chart on the edition -> a reading of anything beyond the numbers the composer already wrote into the page
  witness 2026-09-25 the kept-per-day chart drew from a data-bf-series block the composer emitted, with the numbers remaining in the document whether or not the organ ever bound
  binding scripts/publish-edition.mjs
  binding site/matrix/client-organs.js

interaction estate-edition-publishes-territory-hosts
  source estate-edition
  destination web-address-edge
  relation publishes_one_retained_edition_per_declared_territory
  preserves the exact retained items selected, published magazine profile, territory name and public provenance boundary
  drops publisher adoption, endorsement, source freshness, editorial approval and any authority to republish externally
  forbidden_inference a compiled static edition at a public host -> any publisher approved the arrangement or any story remains current
  invalidates_on retained item material, published presentation templates, edition policy or the publication day changing
  witness scripts/tests/publish_edition.test.mjs
  binding scripts/publish_estate.sh
  binding scripts/publish-edition.mjs
